From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Focus the window a sync asks for, whatever is queued

A Wayland window's activation is settled once a wl_display.sync after
the keyboard's enter or leave comes back, and Qt 6.12.0 then asks for
a focus change only when the window it wants differs from
QGuiApplication::focusWindow(). That function changes only once the
window-system queue is processed. When a surface's leave and enter
come close together, the leave's sync can queue "no window focused",
and the enter's sync come back before that is processed: it finds the
window still focused and asks nothing, so the queued change lands
last and the window stays inactive while it holds the keyboard. The
shell's launcher, given the keys again 39 ms after giving them up,
then never took a key until it was closed.

Comparing with the window the last sync asked for as well sends the
enter's change behind the leave's. A change asked twice is harmless:
processing a focus change to the window already focused returns at
once.

--- a/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylanddisplay.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylanddisplay.cpp
@@ -1076,8 +1076,13 @@
     QWindow *activeWindow = mActiveWindows.empty() ? nullptr : mActiveWindows.last()->window();
     if (mActiveSubSurface)
         activeWindow = mActiveSubSurface->window();
-    if (activeWindow != QGuiApplication::focusWindow())
+    // focusWindow() changes only once the queue is processed, so a leave's sync and an enter's
+    // answered before then would find the window still focused and send nothing, leaving the
+    // leave's queued change last. Comparing with what was last asked too sends the enter's.
+    if (activeWindow != QGuiApplication::focusWindow() || activeWindow != mFocusAsked) {
+        mFocusAsked = activeWindow;
         QWindowSystemInterface::handleFocusWindowChanged(activeWindow);
+    }
 }
 
 const wl_callback_listener QWaylandDisplay::syncCallbackListener = {
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylanddisplay_p.h
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylanddisplay_p.h
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@
 class QSocketNotifier;
 class QPlatformScreen;
 class QPlatformPlaceholderScreen;
+class QWindow;
 
 namespace QtWayland {
     class zwp_text_input_manager_v1;
@@ -393,6 +394,8 @@
     QList<QWaylandWindow *> mActiveWindows;
     QPointer<QWaylandWindow> mActiveSubSurface;
     struct wl_callback *mSyncCallback = nullptr;
+    // The window the last sync asked to be focused, which focusWindow() may not show yet.
+    QPointer<QWindow> mFocusAsked;
     static const wl_callback_listener syncCallbackListener;
     bool mWaylandTryReconnect = false;
     bool mPreferWlrDataControl = false;
